WD1770 READ ADDRESS race test by Kieran Connell (Bitshifters), for the BBC Master.
Source: https://bitshifters.github.io/content/wip/rdaddr-race.ssd
License: MIT (below)

Cut down from an old version of phX's chained-NMI disc driver: it seeks to
track 1, then issues 100 READ ADDRESS commands, each from the previous one's
INTRQ NMI, and prints RESULT: PASS or RESULT: HANG on MODE 7 row 22. A real
Master says HANG: INTRQ arrives so soon after the last ID byte's DRQ that the
driver's NMIs nest and the chain stops.
https://github.com/mattgodbolt/jsbeeb/issues/1850 has the story.

